cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or reference this work, please cite it as below."
title: "ecoPrimals: Sovereign Scientific Computing in Pure Rust"
type: software
authors:
  - alias: ecoPrimal
    email: eco.primal@pm.me
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-2141-0321"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ecoPrimals"
url: "https://sporeprint.primals.eco"
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
keywords:
  - scientific computing
  - GPU computing
  - Rust
  - WGSL
  - WebGPU
  - bioinformatics
  - lattice QCD
  - DADA2
  - vendor-agnostic
  - reproducible science
  - sovereign computing
  - distributed computing
abstract: >-
  ecoPrimals is a sovereign scientific computing ecosystem written in pure Rust.
  It provides GPU-accelerated computation via WebGPU/WGSL across NVIDIA, AMD,
  and Intel GPUs without CUDA or vendor SDKs. The ecosystem includes validated
  pipelines for 16S rRNA bioinformatics (DADA2-compatible), lattice QCD on
  consumer GPUs, pharmacometrics, and 7 additional scientific domains.
  All components are self-hosted, reproducible, and verifiable.
date-released: "2026-07-30"
